  "reviewNote": "M6: Google runtime and its single-provider tests extracted. Shared Google/Vertex algorithms remain owned here; native configuration uses the core HTTP client. Upstream baselines, capabilities and deferred behavior are unchanged. 2026-11-01: reviewed @ai-sdk/google 4.0.105 -> 4.0.109 archives and release-matched tests (612be2311464804d1e4897afacbf8f3fc2f6d9e3 -> 9b603d36186b75e58d5479445a96c76f6e2d2700). Ported changed convert-to-google-messages, google-json-accumulator and google-language-model test deltas in Weekly20261101GoogleTests: typed/validated video metadata and namespace precedence, final string closure, Gemini reasoning minimums and warnings. Async credential resolution covers HTTP continuations, files/batch/interactions and existing media paths; local rotation tests include generation, streaming and file polling. Model-catalog documentation declarations retain the native capability architecture; no native catalog API was invented. Existing realtime and speech-translation product gaps remain; JS resolver/type changes for these unexposed products are out of scope. 2026-11-08: reviewed @ai-sdk/google 4.0.109 -> 4.0.114 published source/declarations and matching-release tests. Ported signed empty text/reasoning replay, streamed text/tool order and terminal partial calls, sparse-index bounds, RPC status retryability, first namespace resolution, provider tool NONE filtering, Interactions labels/tool mapping and speech language. Added native Gemini Live client-secret/server WebSocket codec with per-session turn/transcript state and same-frame usage. Native JSONValue excludes JS cycles/BigInt/toJSON; unchanged browser capture/playback, separate Google transcription and speech translation remain gaps. No complete/live parity claim. 2026-11-14: reviewed @ai-sdk/google 4.0.114 -> 4.0.120 published archives/declarations and exact matching-release tests (0f3a85f92d1ce06ccde01d662407ef83e097a712 -> 8bc7652cdb13fc84722666eb93f45acd0d131eee). Package-specific changes, translated tests, known gaps and compatibility decisions are recorded in Docs/WeeklyUpstreamAudit20261114.json; package README describes consumer behavior. This delta review does not claim whole-package or live-service parity."
